  "body": "## Two small, defended changes rather than a rewrite\n\nBoth views were **already designed** — the Guide's sticky scrollspy TOC has been there since 4.23.0 (PR #29) and the Get Started cards since 4.29.0. The useful work was auditing them against a design plan, not replacing work that holds up.\n\n**Get Started.** The \"N of M essential steps done\" line was plain muted text carrying the only number on the page. It is now a label plus a filled track, width driven by the same ratio, with `role=\"progressbar\"` and matching aria values. A bar shares the step list's own vertical axis, so it reads as the list being filled in rather than a widget parked above it.\n\nA donut with a percentage in the middle was considered and **rejected** — for that same axis reason, and because a big number in a ring is the stock answer.\n\n**Guide.** An \"On this page\" eyebrow above the TOC rail, reusing the existing global `.eyebrow` class rather than inventing type, so the rail reads as deliberate wayfinding instead of a bare list of links.\n\nTabs-instead-of-scroll was considered and rejected: tabs hide how much is left, break find-on-page, and kill deep links like `#guide-cli` — all of which matter more for \"reference read while stuck\" than novelty would gain.\n\n## Cut during self-critique\n\nThe progress bar briefly had an `is-complete` state that swapped the fill to a gradient on finishing. It used only existing tokens, but it added a visual event carrying nothing the bar's fullness did not already say. Removed from **both** the CSS and the JS branch that set it, rather than left as dead weight — verified gone from source, not merely unreferenced.\n\n## Found while auditing, not designed\n\n- `.guide-toc a:focus-visible` changed only its background, so **keyboard focus was invisible on every TOC link**, while every other control in the app gets a 2px accent outline.\n- The highlight-pulse animation and the progress transition had no `prefers-reduced-motion` coverage.\n\n## Palette and type are inherited, deliberately\n\nThese are two views inside a shipped dashboard. A new face or hue for two of them would break the one thing holding the product together. That is the decision, not an omission.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\n$ uv run ty check\nAll checks passed!\n\n$ env -u ENABLE_WEB_SERVER_TOOLS -u EXA_API_KEY uv run pytest tests/api/test_admin.py tests/api/test_admin_onboarding.py tests/config/test_onboarding.py -q\n103 passed in 24.96s\n```\n\n`node --check` clean. Class cross-check in both directions shows no orphans. The state machine in `renderOnboarding` is untouched — confirmed by diffing for the expand/advance identifiers, which return nothing.\n\nThe CSS conflict against 4.35.0's failover rules was resolved by keeping both blocks: braces balance and every rule from each side is present.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- **No browser available**, so the bar's proportions and the eyebrow's spacing against existing TOC padding are read from the box model, not seen.\n- **The Guide's bundled screenshots still show the v4.15.0 UI** and are now further out of date after this week's Model Config and Web Search redesigns. Not addressed here — refreshing them needs a live server with real traffic — but it is the largest remaining problem with that page, and worth doing before the screenshots mislead someone.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
